# CVE-2026-14456 (OpenSSL, libssl3/libcrypto3 3.5.7-r1, fixed upstream in 3.5.8).
# Not exploitable - unbounded memory growth in the OpenSSL QUIC server's incoming
# channel queue. nginx in this image serves static files over plain HTTP on 8080,
# does not terminate TLS (the OpenShift router does) and never opens an OpenSSL
# QUIC listener, so the affected path does not exist at runtime.
# Remove this block once the base image ships OpenSSL >= 3.5.8-r0.
CVE-2026-14456

# CVE-2026-85091 (zlib 1.3.2-r0, no fixed package in Alpine v3.23 or edge).
# Not exploitable - heap buffer overflow in gz_vacate() on a stalled non-blocking
# gzwrite(), reachable only through zlib's gz* file-handle API. nginx compresses
# responses through the deflate stream API and never calls gzprintf()/gzvprintf();
# this image does not enable gzip at all.
# Remove this block once the base image ships a fixed zlib.
CVE-2026-85091
